  volume                  = {216},
  abbrev_source_title = {Meas J Int Meas Confed},
  abstract                = {In machinery fault diagnosis, most of the entropy features used were proposed for time series signals, while much key information of vibration signals, including fault information, can only be disclosed on the Time-Frequency Image (TFI). Besides, in the TFI of a signal, the first region to be noticed is generally the region with a large amplitude, but the difference between many signals lies in these details whose amplitude is small. Aiming at this issue, in this paper, we propose a novel entropy feature, named Multislice Time-Frequency Image Entropy (MTFIE), to capture the low-amplitude details embedded in a signal and to characterize the frequency stability and frequency mutability of the signal. The proposed MTFIE feature, combined with a Neural Network (NN)-based classifier, is constructed as a fault diagnostic method for railway wheels. The results show that the MTIFIE-NN method can achieve excellent results under both ideal and real-world operating conditions. © 2023 Elsevier Ltd},
