  pages = {507--518},
  volume                  = {35},
  abbrev_source_title = {Hupo Kexue/J. Lake Sc.},
  abstract                = {Harmfu algae booms in Three Gorges Reservoir (TGR) have become the most major environmental and ecological probem. Despte broad recogntion that hydrological manpuation, warming climate and nutrien loadng promote the ntensity and frequency of boom events, the main probem s still no science-based framework for evaluating the causal relationshps between environmental factors and phytopankton bomass by using field observation data. Thus, as a case study, a noninear time-series causality analysis framework was used o reveal the phytopankton response in he TGR, Chna. Two samping stations, named Lake Gaoy-angpng and Lake Hanfeng, were used o reconstruct the dynamics of real-world environmental systems with eleven parameters from June 2007 to September 2018 Snguar spectrum analysis isolated low-dmensional, determinstic signals for chorophyll-a(Ch.a) dynamics and other candidate drivers. Causal analysis with convergent cross-mapping ( CCM) provided strong evidence that temperature, sunshine hours, precipitation, discharge in the tributary, and water level of TCR systematically influenced phytoplankton bi-omass dynamics in Lake Caoyangping. In contrast, total nitrogen (TN) and total phosphorus (TP) showed a causal relationship with Chi.a only in Lake Hanfeng, and the effect of TN on Chi.a was more significant than that of TP. Finally, the research compares the nonlinear CCM analysis with the linear Pearson correlation analysis and Granger causality test. It confirms that the nonlinear causality method has more advantage in causal discovery based on long time-series monitoring data. Overall, this study provides a case for causal modelling of water ecosystems and a new research perspective for evaluating the environmental drivers of harmful algae blooms in TOR by using long-term observational data. ©2023 by Journal of Lake Sciences.},
  affiliation             = {School of Computer Science, China West Normal University, Nanchong, 637009, China; Chongqing Institute of Green and Intelligent Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences, CAS Key Lab on Reservoir Environment, Chongqing, 400714, China; College of Computer Science and Technology, Chongqing University of Posts and Telecommunications, Chongqing, 400065, China; School of Artificial Intelligence, Chongqing University of Education, Chongqing, 400065, China},
