  editor              = {Zhang J.},
  note                = {cited By 0},
  pages = {509--515},
  publisher           = {Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.},
  abbrev_source_title = {Proc. - Int. Conf. Commun., Image Signal Process., CCISP},
  abstract            = {The subway sliding door system is an important part of the subway for ensuring the safe operation. To address the issues of high cost and low efficiency of the current subway sliding door fault detection methods, a fault diagnosis method based on motor current signal is proposed in this paper. The original motor current data are first preprocessed and segmented, then Multiscale Permutation Entropy (MPE) features are extracted from each segment. Fisher discriminant criterion is employed to further select the important features. Random forest model is utilized for fault detection, whose parameters are optimized by Seagull Optimization Algorithm (SOA). Experiments with real data have been conducted to test the proposed method. A remarkable prediction accuracy of 94% have been achieved in the results. The effectiveness of the proposed method has been verified. © 2023 IEEE.},
