  number                  = {11},
  volume                  = {32},
  abbrev_source_title = {Chaos},
  abstract                = {This is a review of group entropy and its application to permutation complexity. Specifically, we revisit a new approach to the notion of complexity in the time series analysis based on both permutation entropy and group entropy. As a result, the permutation entropy rate can be extended from deterministic dynamics to random processes. More generally, our approach provides a unified framework to discuss chaotic and random behaviors. © 2022 Author(s).},
