  volume                  = {111},
  abbrev_source_title = {Mech. Mach. Sci.},
  abstract                = {Entropy is an effective method to measure the randomness of signals and the sudden change of nonlinear dynamics. In order to suppress the noise interference of rolling bearing fault signal, a new feature is proposed, namely the composite multiscale slope entropy (CMSlE). In further, an approach based on the CMSlE and principal component analysis (PCA) is proposed to assess the performance state of rolling bearings, and the approach is validated with the experimental data. The results show that the composite slope entropy of each scale can clearly express the performance state of rolling bearings from aspects of sensitivity and overall trend; the proposed method can give a comprehensive monitoring indicator to express the performance state of rolling bearings. © 2022, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd.},
