  abbrev_source_title = {IEEE Int. Conf. Artif. Intell. Comput. Appl., ICAICA},
  abstract            = {In this paper, a algorithm named fractional order coded permutation entropy (FCPE) is proposed by introducing fractional calculus into coded permutation entropy (CPE). A Logistic map is used to study the performance of FCPE under different fractional order parameter in dynamic changes detection. Then, FCPE is applied to detect three types of rolling bearing fault signals. Simulation results show that compared with CPE, fractional permutation entropy (FPE) and weighted fractional permutation entropy (WFPE), FCPE can effectively amplify the dynamic changes of the system and improve the detection ability of abnormal changes when suitable fractional order parameter is selected. For the same rolling bearing fault, the detection performance of FCPE is more significant compared to other three methods. © 2021 IEEE.},
