  abstract          = {Complexity measures for time series that applied to real world data were introduced. It was shown that the complexity behaved similar to Lyapunov exponents and was useful in the presence of dynamical or observational noise. Permutation entropy was found to be an appropriate complexity measure for chaotic time series. Various advantages of the method like simplicity, fast calculation, robustness, and invariance with respect to nonlinear monotonous transformations were presented.},
